  ],
  "dct_accessRights_s": "Public",
  "dct_creator_sm": [
    "Newfoundland and Labrador Fisheries, Forestry and Agriculture GeoHub."
  ],
  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>This feature layer contains Resource Roads in Newfoundland and Labrador.</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'><br /></span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-weight:bold;'>This data is for illustrative purposes only.</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-weight:bold;'><br /></span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit;'></span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>Access definitions (imagine you just leased a brand new pickup truck):</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'><br /></span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>Open = road is easily accessible by 2WD vehicles</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>Limited = road is rough and/or slightly grown in (likely need 4x4)</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>ATV = road only accessible by ATV</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>Not Passable = road is not passable (grown in and/or road condition)</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>Unknown = unknown road access</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'>T'Railway = ATV/Snowmobile permitted; Need permit from Provincial Parks for passenger vehicles</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:12pt;'><br /></span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'>This feature layer is the authoritative resource roads layer for the Labrador portion of the province. It is administered by the Forest Engineering and Industry Services division and provides viewing and geoprocessing functionality. </p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><br /></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'>For further information, please direct inquiries to the Forest Engineering and Industry Services Division of the Department of Forestry, Agriculture and Lands.</p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><br /></p><div style='font-size:12pt;'><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><b><u>Attribute Descriptions</u></b></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><b><br /></b></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><b>Access</b></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'>By default, the resource road layer is symbolized by <i>access</i>. Access is an estimated assessment of how easy a road can be traveled. For example, imagine you leased a new vehicle - how easy is the road to drive without damaging the vehicle.</p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><br /></p><table border='0' cellpadding='0' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse; width:620pt;' width='825'><tbody><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt; width:103pt;' width='137'><b>Code*</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:137pt;' width='182'><b>Code Description</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:380pt;' width='506'><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>1</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Open</td><td style='border-left:none;'>2WD vehicles. No issue with access.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>2</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Limited</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Road is rough and/or grown in (scratches). May require 4x4 vehicle.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>3</td><td style='border-left:none;'>ATV</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Accessible with ATV or UTV only. Not accessible by passenger vehicle.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>4</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Not Passable</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Not passable due to assessed conditions (e.g. decommissioned).</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>5</td><td style='border-left:none;'>T'Railway</td><td style='border-left:none;'>T'Railway Provincial Park (requires permit to access with passenger vehicle).</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>6</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Unknown</td><td style='border-left:none;'> </td></tr></tbody></table><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><b><br /></b></p><b>Authority</b></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'>The <i>road authority</i> attribute identifies the group, organization or entity responsible for managing and maintaining the road network<i>. </i>This may include the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador (Crown, TI), industry (<i>i.e.</i> CBPPL), or a cabin association.</div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><b><br /></b><table border='0' cellpadding='0' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse; width:561pt;' width='748'><tbody><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt; width:56pt;' width='75'><b>Code*</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:125pt;' width='167'><b>Code Description</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:380pt;' width='506'><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>1</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Crown</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Dept of Fisheries and Land Resources (NL Forest Service).</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>2</td><td style='border-left:none;'>CBPPL</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Road managed by CBPPL (Tenure).</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>3</td><td style='border-left:none;'>TI</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Dept of Transportation &amp; Infrastructure.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>4</td><td style='border-left:none;'>NL Hydro</td><td style='border-left:none;'>e.g. hydro dams, lines.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>5</td><td style='border-left:none;'>NLSF</td><td style='border-left:none;'>NL Snowmobile Federation (e.g. groomed snowmobile trail).</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>6</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Emera</td><td style='border-left:none;'>e.g. Hydro transmission line.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>7</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Contractor-Built-Road</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Specific to Commercial Cutting Permit Holders (Contractor-Built-Road).</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>8</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Private</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Privately owned road.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>9</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Cabin Owner/Association</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Cabin owner or association maintains/manages road.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>10</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Unknown</td><td style='border-left:none;'> </td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>11</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Other</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Other user maintaining/managing road.</td></tr></tbody></table><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><br /></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><b>Road Class</b></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'>The <i>Road Class</i> attribute identifies the type and purpose of the road segment. This attribute describes whether a road is designed to provide general access to a forest management district, or to provide limited access within an operating area (<i>i.e.</i> to access an area identified for commercial harvest.)</p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'><br /></p><table border='0' cellpadding='0' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse; width:620pt;' width='825'><tbody><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt; width:103pt;' width='137'><b>Code*</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:137pt;' width='182'><b>Code Description</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:380pt;' width='506'><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>1</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Capital</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Provide general access to FMD as a whole. Always connect to pavement.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>2</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Access</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Provide access to general areas within FMD. Branch off of Capital or pavement.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>3</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Operational</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Provide access within operating areas (get at wood).</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>4</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Historic</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Historic road.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>5</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Unclassified</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Unclassified or unknown Class.</td></tr></tbody></table><br /><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; text-align:justify;'></p></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><b>Surface</b></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'>The <i>road surface</i> attribute identifies the material of the road surface. This may include gravel, paved, or another composite material (<i>i.e. </i>chip seal).</div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><br /></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><table border='0' cellpadding='0' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse; width:620pt;' width='825'><tbody><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt; width:103pt;' width='137'><b>Code*</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:137pt;' width='182'><b>Code Description</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:380pt;' width='506'><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>1</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Gravel</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Gravel surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>2</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Paved</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Pavement surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>3</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Other</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Other surface (e.g. chip seal).</td></tr></tbody></table><br /></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><b>Specification</b></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'>The <i>road specification</i> attribute identifies the specification that the road is built to adhere to. The specification assesses the width of the road surface and is classified using an alphabetical attribute with A being the widest and D being the narrowest. </div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><br /></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><table border='0' cellpadding='0' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse; width:620pt;' width='825'><tbody><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt; width:103pt;' width='137'><b>Code*</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:137pt;' width='182'><b>Code Description</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:380pt;' width='506'><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>1</td><td style='border-left:none;'>A</td><td style='border-left:none;'>9 m wide driving surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>2</td><td style='border-left:none;'>B</td><td style='border-left:none;'>7.5 m wide driving surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>3</td><td style='border-left:none;'>C-2</td><td style='border-left:none;'>6 m wide driving surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>4</td><td style='border-left:none;'>C</td><td style='border-left:none;'>5 m wide driving surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>5</td><td style='border-left:none;'>C-1</td><td style='border-left:none;'>4 m wide driving surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>6</td><td style='border-left:none;'>D</td><td style='border-left:none;'>3.5-4.5 m wide driving surface.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>7</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Unknown</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Unknown road specification.</td></tr></tbody></table><br /></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><b>Driving Speed</b></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'>The <i>driving speed </i>attribute is a rating (where applicable) of the speed of travel. It is an estimation of speed that a road surface can sustain safely.</div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><br /></div><div style='font-size:12pt;'><table border='0' cellpadding='0' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse; width:620pt;' width='825'><tbody><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt; width:103pt;' width='137'><b>Code*</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:137pt;' width='182'><b>Code Description</b></td><td style='border-left:none; width:380pt;' width='506'><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>1</td><td style='border-left:none;'>55</td><td style='border-left:none;'>55 km/hr.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>2</td><td style='border-left:none;'>50</td><td style='border-left:none;'>50 km/hr.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>3</td><td style='border-left:none;'>30</td><td style='border-left:none;'>30 km/hr.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>4</td><td style='border-left:none;'>25</td><td style='border-left:none;'>25 km/hr.</td></tr><tr height='20' style='height:15pt;'><td height='20' style='height:15pt;'>5</td><td style='border-left:none;'>0</td><td style='border-left:none;'>Unknown.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:justify;'><br /></p>"
